//@version=5
// NON-VACUITY CONTROL FOR THE RENDER GATE -- this script MUST NOT draw.
// Its window reaches back further than any history the chart loads, so every
// bar of its column is NaN, `planBindings` gives the plot no series, and
// `legendChips` stamps the chip `data-computed="false"`. If the harness reports
// this as CHART_RENDERABLE, the render gate cannot distinguish drawing from not
// drawing and no number it produces means anything.
indicator("Control Window Exceeds History", overlay = false)
plot(ta.sma(close, 100000), title = "Empty", color = color.purple, linewidth = 2)
